 {"q": "The detail that the letters were \"full of weather\" suggests that the letters were:", "c": ["superficial, avoiding the important feelings between them.", "mostly concerned with problems at the lighthouse.", "written during storms that damaged the town.", "longer and more detailed than ordinary letters."], "cat": "CS", "x": "They were \"polite and short\"; talking about weather means avoiding what they really meant."},
 {"q": "The father's first words to the narrator are most likely intended to show that he:", "c": ["expresses his feelings indirectly, through practical matters they share.", "has forgotten that his daughter had been away.", "is angry that she came without warning.", "wants her to leave as soon as possible."], "cat": "IKI", "x": "Instead of an emotional greeting, he raises the lamp, an engineering problem she can help with, and she accepts."},
